From 6f9414ce58445ec30c7be4778d1bf0971d075e03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:05:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/57] hw/rtc: MCP79411 RTCC and the RTC 6 Click

- mchp-mcp79411 (MCP7941X data sheet DS20002266H): one device answering
  0x6F (RTCC registers, 64-byte SRAM) and 0x57 (EEPROM, protected block
  with the EUI-48, STATUS) through its own match_and_add. Timekeeping on
  the virtual clock once ST is set (BCD, 12/24 h, weekdays, month
  lengths, leap years, OSCRUN), power-on reset values, two alarms with
  all masks and ALMPOL logic (ALMxIF set again while the match
  persists), the open-drain MFP (alarm output, 1 Hz square wave, OUT),
  EEPROM page writes at STOP with a 5 ms busy time, block protection and
  the 0x55/0xAA unlock for the protected block. "time" (read/load),
  "running", "eui48".
- mikrobus: "rtc6" (schematic v100): MFP on INT with R2 10k pull-up.
- qtests: time and rollovers (new year, leap day, 12-hour), ST, alarm
  latching and polarity, square wave, SRAM wrap, EEPROM busy, page wrap,
  block protection, unlock; on mikroBUS 3 of the Nano Base too.

Not checked against a physical RTC 6 Click.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
