@@ -118,6 +118,17 @@ resistors are modelled (from their schematics, v100).
   DATA_READY/OVERRUN/WATERMARK and the INT pins are modelled; tap,
   activity and free-fall detection and the FIFO modes are not.
 
+``rtc6``
+  RTC 6 Click: an MCP79411 RTCC (``mchp-mcp79411``) at I2C 0x6F (RTCC
+  registers, 64 bytes of SRAM) and 0x57 (1 Kbit EEPROM, the protected
+  block with the EUI-48, STATUS), its open-drain MFP on INT (R2 10 kOhm
+  pull-up). The clock counts virtual time once ST is set, from the
+  power-on date 2001-01-01; alarms, the 1 Hz square wave and the general
+  purpose output drive MFP; EEPROM writes take 5 ms. QOM properties
+  ``time`` ("YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS", read or load), ``running`` and
+  ``eui48``. Trimming, power-fail time-stamps and the faster square waves
+  are not modelled.
+
 SPI Clicks on both headers share the SPI bus; each listens only while its
 own CS is low (or, for the 74HC595 and MAX7219, latches on its own CS).
 
